From d559513bf1eda56830143d86eedef7544258b61e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:08:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: Wireless > Settings replaces the General and
 Professional tabs

One page, 38 rows x 3 radios, replaces Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp,
Advanced_WAdvanced_Content.asp and Reaper_WiFiPro.asp (deleted). Network
name, security, Wi-Fi 6/7 mode and Smart Connect stay on the Network menu;
every other radio setting from the ASUS Professional page is here per band,
locked only where stock locks it, greyed with no reason text.

httpd: new SSI wlpro_chanspecs() emits the per-radio chanspec list from
wlN_chansps (filled by the prebuilt ej_wl_chanspecs) so the channel and
bandwidth rows offer what the driver reports; wlpro_nv_fields grows to 37
keys. reaper_inject SUP-redirects the three old pages to the new one;
Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp leaves reaper_css_only so the bounce reaches
it.

Channel rows fold into wlN_chanspec at apply as the General tab did (2.4 GHz
<ch>l|u plus wlN_nctrlsb, 5 GHz <ch>/<bw>, 6 GHz 6g<ch>/320-1|2). The
scheduler writes the V2 wlN_sched_v2 off-time rules that rc/watchdog reads
on this build. A forced value is written at apply as a derived heal when
nvram disagrees (WMM on, MU-MIMO from OFDMA, TX bursting off under
pre-emptive BT, beamforming under MU-MIMO, scheduler off under MLO), as the
11ax heal already was.

The enhanced select menus ignore clicks and scrolls inside the open list (a
long channel list vanished when its scrollbar was touched; WiFiPro had the
same bug). menuTree gets one Settings tab; the dashboard rail and the WPS
page's two links point at the new page (SDN.asp for authentication).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
